{"commit": "cc68ae4f426d48eb69be9178c28440585c0c32fc", "id": "cc68ae4f426d48eb69be9178c28440585c0c32fc-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Proposal names no upstream test", "repo": "https://github.com/toml-rs/toml", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260924T005753Z-a9b97836", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/cc68ae4f426d48eb69be9178c28440585c0c32fc-1/20260924T005753Z-a9b97836/origin.json": "26b2b562e36136ab87c9c8cbeb9c7a2aa21185ccd7ea3f16b9624b93a76fa0a9", "evidence/cc68ae4f426d48eb69be9178c28440585c0c32fc-1/20260924T005753Z-a9b97836/proposal.json": "bd6ad6dd92393a3f2b6b13765f58d7a4700b181d02474a26e95228cf885383d5"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "toml_edit", "status": "blocked", "subject": "fix(lex): Don't loop over ')' for forever", "summary": "A `)` byte was accidentally included in the lexer's `TOKEN_START` set. When `lex_atom` saw a `)`, `offset_for` returned 0 (the current position is already a token-start), nothing was consumed, and the outer iterator re-entered `lex_atom` on the same byte forever. The fix drops `)` from `TOKEN_START`.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:57:53.641291+00:00"}
